From edbc84a985cf717b34dc3f8421896f2ef4f48c60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bcup02 <55205420+bcup02@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 22:59:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gs): legacy update paths set @ format BEFORE setValue
 (v0.13.4) (#9)

v0.13.3 gap. handleLegacyUpdateByTradeId / handleLegacyUpdateByKey called
cell.setNumberFormat('@') AFTER cell.setValue(). Sheets first parses a
datetime-shaped string into a Date serial -- and if that cell already
carried a date number-format that hides seconds, the seconds are dropped
at the display layer -- then setNumberFormat('@') freezes the already
re-formatted display string as text. So "2026-08-20 2:25:00" written into
a Date-value cell became "2026-08-20 2:25".

Reorder to @ format first, then setValue, in both update paths.
handleLegacyAppend already sets @ (in the forEach) before range.setValues,
and v2 writeProjection is already @-then-setValue -- neither changed.

- node test: the sheet stub records setValue / setNumberFormat call order;
  update_by_trade_id / update_by_key assert setNumberFormat precedes
  setValue for a datetime-shaped column, and setValue-only for a plain one.
- 0.13.3 -> 0.13.4; release-log entry.

Consumers do not bump the pin (.gs is pasted manually). The operator
re-pastes google_ledger_receiver.gs -> Manage deployments -> new version.
The 3 seconds-dropped rows are re-fixed by the momentum rewrite tool once
canonical_taipei also accepts "YYYY-MM-DD H:MM".

Co-authored-by: bcup02 <columnbb@gmail.com>
Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
